.TH "PERCH-MAIL-CAPS" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail\-caps \- show the SMTP extensions advertised by a submission server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail caps [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Connect to the configured submission server, perform EHLO, and print the advertised extensions. No message is sent and no credentials are used.
.PP
Aliases: capabilities.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The local perch relay advertises PIPELINING, 8BITMIME, ENHANCEDSTATUSCODES, SIZE, SMTPUTF8, STARTTLS, and AUTH on loopback or TLS.
.IP \(bu 2
It does not expose DSN, CHUNKING, BINARYMIME, REQUIRETLS, or DELIVERBY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-server, \-S <value>
SMTP submission server (smtps://host, smtp://host, or host[:port]); defaults from \-\-config
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-plaintext
connect to SMTP without TLS (use only on trusted networks)
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-starttls
require STARTTLS for SMTP
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-implicit\-tls
use implicit TLS for SMTP (usually port 465)
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-insecure
skip SMTP TLS certificate verification
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-ca\-file <value>
PEM CA bundle used to verify the SMTP server certificate
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail caps

perch mail caps \-\-smtp\-server smtp.mxraven.email:587
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1)
